command       : .venv/Scripts/python.exe scripts/compare_hawkes_windows.py --points 24 --windows 750,1000
why           : in run 10 (60/250/500d) out-of-sample per-bar NLL fell MONOTONICALLY with
                window length (0.23221 -> 0.17622 -> 0.13253), so the best value sat at the
                EDGE of the grid and the optimum was not bracketed. Selecting a boundary
                point would be an unjustified choice. This extends the grid until either the
                optimum is interior or the corpus binds. Same script, same pre-registered
                selection rule, same 24 evaluation points - only the grid changes.
corpus bound  : 2,850 sessions; a 1000d window + 5d OOS leaves ~1,845 sessions for the
                24 evaluation points, so both candidates are admissible.
side effects  : none - read-only script, reads the regenerated p1_data.pkl cache
